   "source": [
    "# 🏏 SupeRR Selector Season 2: Phase 3 — Context Normalization, Clutch Deltas & Empirical Bayes\n",
    "## Eliminating Sample Noise & Environment Bias in Sports ML\n",
    "\n",
    "### What You Will Learn in This Phase:\n",
    "1. **Diagnostic Auditing in ML**: How inspecting our initial rankings uncovered two subtle data-science traps (The *Phase-Mismatch Trap* & The *Competition-Format Bias*).\n",
    "2. **Environment Normalization (RAE & RSAE)**: Adjusting runs scored and conceded relative to `(Competition Format × Innings Phase)` benchmarks.\n",
    "3. **The Clutch Delta ($\Delta$)**: Measuring whether a player elevates their context-adjusted performance under high leverage.\n",
    "4. **Empirical Bayes Shrinkage (James-Stein Estimator)**: Dynamically stabilizing small-sample estimates toward the population prior $\\mu_0$."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "sys.path.append('..')\n",
    "\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "from src.ml.pressure_ranker import run_context_normalized_ml_ranking\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\")\n",
    "plt.rcParams[\"figure.figsize\"] = (12, 6)\n",
    "plt.rcParams[\"font.size\"] = 11"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "### Step 1: The Two Traps Uncovered During Diagnostic Auditing\n",
    "When we ran our naive baseline comparison, we immediately scrutinized the rankings using cricketing intuition and discovered two critical modeling bugs:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Competition-Format Bias (IPL vs. T20I):**\n",
    "   * In IPL/Franchise T20s (`match_format == 'T20'`), the implied Strike Rate is **139.46** (Economy: **8.37 RPO**).\n",
    "   * In International T20Is (`match_format == 'T20I'`), the implied Strike Rate is **129.34** (Economy: **7.76 RPO**).\n",
    "   * Without adjustment, T20I bowlers enjoy an artificial $+0.61$ economy advantage over IPL bowlers!\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **The Phase-Mismatch Trap (Why Jasprit Bumrah Dropped in Naive Deltas):**\n",
    "   * Bowlers like Jasprit Bumrah are saved specifically for high-leverage **Death Overs (16–20)**, where the league par economy is ~10.3 RPO.\n",
    "   * Bumrah's normal economy in overs 1–6 is `6.99`. His pressure economy in overs 16–20 is `7.73`.\n",
    "   * A naive delta (`base_econ - hp_econ`) produces $6.99 - 7.73 = -0.74$, punishing Bumrah for bowling in the hardest overs!\n",
    "   * **The Fix:** Compare every delivery against the **expected par for that exact Format and Phase**:\n",
    "     $$\\text{RSAE}_{\\text{bowl}} = E[\\text{Runs Conceded} \\mid \\text{Format}, \\text{Phase}] - \\text{Actual Runs Conceded}$$"
   ]
  },
