  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "### Step 2: Visualizing Empirical Bayes Shrinkage (The Shrinkage Funnel)\n",
    "How do we ensure a player who bowled 10 lucky overs doesn't beat Jasprit Bumrah or Sunil Narine?\n",
    "\n",
    "Using **Empirical Bayes Shrinkage**:\n",
    "$$\\hat{\\theta}_i = \\left(\\frac{n_i}{n_i + v_0}\\right)\\bar{x}_i + \\left(\\frac{v_0}{n_i + v_0}\\right)\\mu_0$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's plot **Raw Observed Performance** vs. **Bayesian-Shrunk Performance** as a function of sample size ($n_i$)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "full_bat = pd.read_csv('../data/processed/ml_full_batters_under_pressure.csv')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n",
    "plt.scatter(full_bat['hp_balls'], full_bat['raw_hp_sr'], alpha=0.4, color='gray', label='Raw Observed Pressure SR')\n",
    "plt.scatter(full_bat['hp_balls'], full_bat['bayes_hp_sr'], alpha=0.8, color='#EA1A80', label='Bayesian-Shrunk Pressure SR')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Highlight top 5 batters\n",
    "for _, row in full_bat.head(5).iterrows():\n",
    "    plt.annotate(row['striker_name'], (row['hp_balls'], row['bayes_hp_sr']), \n",
    "                 textcoords=\"offset points\", xytext=(0, 8), ha='center', fontweight='bold', fontsize=9)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.title('Empirical Bayes Shrinkage Funnel: Eliminating Small-Sample Volatility', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('High-Pressure Balls Faced (Sample Size $n_i$)', fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Strike Rate Under Pressure', fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.legend()\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
